# AVD-AWS-0017: CloudWatch log group is not encrypted with a customer-managed KMS key.
# The AWS managed key is sufficient for this project.

AVD-AWS-0017

# AVD-AWS-0095: Alarm notifications contain resource status metadata, not application payloads.
# CloudWatch publishing to an encrypted topic would require a separately managed KMS key and policy.
AVD-AWS-0095

# AVD-AWS-0066: PassThrough is deliberate so Lambda does not create traces automatically.
# Model input and output tracing remains disabled.
AVD-AWS-0066

# AVD-AWS-0025: DynamoDB uses the AWS managed KMS key for encryption at rest.
# Separate customer-managed key administration is not required for this table.
AVD-AWS-0025

# AVD-AWS-0024: Development data is disposable, so dev disables PITR to reduce cost.
# Production enables PITR in prod.tfvars; the environment contract test checks it.
AVD-AWS-0024
